Q: Remove blank spaces between buttons in HTML, CSS A: <p>Browsers always add spaces between some elements, including buttons. To remove these, you need to set font-size to zero for their parent container. Then, to restore text size inside buttons, set font-size for them.</p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>#stripe {
  font-size: 0;
}

button {
  font-size: 14px; /* Set font size that you need here */
}
</code></pre>
